{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, thanks for getting in touch. I'm afraid we can't set your password to 12345678. Brightline passwords have to be at least 14 characters long, and the help desk never chooses or sees a password you'll keep using.\n\nCould you tell me which of these fits?\n1) You know your current password and just want a new one. You can change it yourself: on your Windows desktop, press Ctrl+Alt+Del, choose 'Change a password', and pick a new one of at least 14 characters that you haven't used recently. A short passphrase of a few unrelated words is easy to remember.\n2) You've forgotten your password and can't sign in. Just reply to let us know. We'll set a temporary password, a technician will call you with it (we never send passwords by email or ticket), and you'll choose your own new password the next time you sign in.\n\nThanks!",
  "internal_note": "Sender is the account owner, writing from her verified email (user_id 11, Receptionist, not VIP). Account is active, not locked: 0 failed sign-ins, no forced password change, sign-in not blocked. Not enrolled in Duo, so self-service reset isn't available. She asked for her password to be set to '12345678'. We can't do that: the help desk can't set a password the user picks, and it breaks the 14-character minimum (KB-003). Her ticket doesn't say she forgot her password or is locked out, so I haven't queued reset_password yet. I asked whether she just wants to change it (she can use Ctrl+Alt+Del herself) or has forgotten it (then queue reset_password and deliver the temporary password by phone, per KB-002). Side note: she isn't enrolled in Duo, so it may be worth suggesting enrollment.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-002",
    "KB-003"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
